      "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
      "text": "If the 'recommended mix' is derived from the same data used to assess adherence and winning, or if it incorporates information that would not be available in real-time decision-making, it will suffer from leakage, leading to artifactual results."
    },
    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "Team winning is a complex outcome. It would be extremely difficult to control for all confounding factors (e.g., team talent, opponent talent, injuries, game context, offensive performance) to isolate the specific impact of adherence to a defensive strategy."
    },
    {
      "code": "RTM_SELECTION",
      "text": "If 'suppression' is defined by extreme performance (e.g., unusually high opponent efficiency on a play type), then any subsequent 'recommended mix' might be subject to regression to the mean, where performance naturally normalizes regardless of strategy adherence."
    },
    {
      "code": "EXPOSURE_SPARSITY",
      "text": "Specific 'suppression-conditional recommended mixes' might occur rarely, leading to sparse data for certain conditions or strategies, making it difficult to draw statistically powerful conclusions."
    },
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
